# This repository is two services, and each one reads its own env file.
# There is nothing to configure at the root — copy the two below instead.
#
#   frontend/.env   (from frontend/.env.example)
#       The Vite SPA. Needs nothing in development: vite.config.ts proxies
#       /api to the backend, so the browser only ever calls relative paths.
#
#   backend/.env    (from backend/.env.example)
#       Everything server-side, in one process on :4000 — auth, AI calling,
#       form-webhook ingestion and the processing worker. Owns the database
#       URL, JWT_SECRET and the encryption keys.
#
# Never commit either: they are gitignored, and between them they hold the
# database password, the JWT signing secret, and the keys that decrypt stored
# provider credentials.
